1
00:00:00,738 --> 00:00:04,046
With tools like LM Studio, but also Ollama,

2
00:00:04,447 --> 00:00:07,530
you can control how the loaded model

3
00:00:07,738 --> 00:00:10,596
generates tokens and therefore its output.

4
00:00:11,415 --> 00:00:14,000
And specifically, you can typically tweak

5
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:17,163
the temperature and values called top-k,

6
00:00:17,356 --> 00:00:20,583
top-p, and sometimes also min-p. But what

7
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:21,884
are these terms about now?

8
00:00:23,152 --> 00:00:25,914
The temperature setting can be used to

9
00:00:26,363 --> 00:00:30,105
modify the probabilities that are assigned

10
00:00:30,201 --> 00:00:33,238
to the different tokens or token candidates.

11
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:36,467
And to understand that, it's important to

12
00:00:36,467 --> 00:00:39,262
understand that these large language models

13
00:00:39,519 --> 00:00:43,262
generate tokens or token candidates. So if

14
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:44,916
we, for example, have a sequence like the

15
00:00:44,916 --> 00:00:45,607
sky is,

16
00:00:46,202 --> 00:00:46,410
then

17
00:00:47,069 --> 00:00:49,816
as a next token or word, the model may

18
00:00:49,816 --> 00:00:51,776
generate blue or clear

19
00:00:52,306 --> 00:00:55,808
or visible or some other word. And each

20
00:00:56,386 --> 00:00:59,095
token it considers has a probability

21
00:00:59,127 --> 00:01:02,093
assigned to it. Now, it's this probability

22
00:01:02,093 --> 00:01:04,625
and this token that is derived by all these

23
00:01:04,738 --> 00:01:07,222
weights, all these parameters that make up

24
00:01:07,222 --> 00:01:09,723
the model. So based on your input, the sky

25
00:01:10,172 --> 00:01:11,599
is, based on these tokens,

26
00:01:12,192 --> 00:01:14,628
these token candidates and their

27
00:01:14,821 --> 00:01:17,690
probabilities are generated by the model.

28
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:20,672
And with temperature, top-k, top-p, and

29
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:24,150
min-p, you can configure which of these

30
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:27,228
possible tokens are actually considered for

31
00:01:27,276 --> 00:01:29,875
sampling. So which tokens are actually

32
00:01:29,907 --> 00:01:32,746
considered to be chosen for the actual

33
00:01:33,019 --> 00:01:34,222
output, so to say.

34
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:37,816
And with temperature, as mentioned, you can

35
00:01:37,928 --> 00:01:40,704
modify these probabilities, for example.

36
00:01:41,378 --> 00:01:44,009
To be precise, if you set a low temperature

37
00:01:44,025 --> 00:01:48,308
value, 0 or 0.1 or something like this,

38
00:01:48,998 --> 00:01:52,480
then differences in probabilities are

39
00:01:52,688 --> 00:01:53,587
exaggerated.

40
00:01:54,116 --> 00:01:56,379
Which means, for example, that blue, which

41
00:01:56,379 --> 00:01:59,315
in my example here has a made-up probability

42
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:00,358
of 45%,

43
00:02:01,593 --> 00:02:03,278
would become even more likely. The

44
00:02:03,342 --> 00:02:06,856
probability might get boosted to 90% or 95%

45
00:02:07,353 --> 00:02:08,139
behind the scenes

46
00:02:08,717 --> 00:02:10,867
after the tokens were generated. So these

47
00:02:10,979 --> 00:02:13,579
tweaks are made after the token candidates

48
00:02:13,627 --> 00:02:16,274
have been generated by the model. So a low

49
00:02:16,274 --> 00:02:18,729
temperature value will boost the likely

50
00:02:18,906 --> 00:02:20,911
probabilities to be even more likely and

51
00:02:21,072 --> 00:02:23,608
make the unlikely probabilities even less

52
00:02:23,737 --> 00:02:25,616
likely. On the other hand, a high

53
00:02:25,744 --> 00:02:28,298
temperature flattens those differences and

54
00:02:28,378 --> 00:02:31,639
leads to more equal probabilities. So again,

55
00:02:31,751 --> 00:02:33,775
in this example with a high temperature

56
00:02:33,775 --> 00:02:34,064
setting,

57
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:38,705
blue might go down from 45% to 20%, but

58
00:02:38,737 --> 00:02:40,970
clear might go up to 20%,

59
00:02:41,628 --> 00:02:42,383
for example.

60
00:02:43,251 --> 00:02:45,306
That's what the temperature setting does.

61
00:02:45,724 --> 00:02:47,892
And we'll see it in action in the next

62
00:02:47,892 --> 00:02:48,599
lecture, of course.

63
00:02:49,595 --> 00:02:51,939
But we don't just have the temperature. We

64
00:02:52,148 --> 00:02:54,461
also, for example, have the top-k value,

65
00:02:54,653 --> 00:02:55,488
which can be set.

66
00:02:56,725 --> 00:02:59,567
And with top-k, we can limit the number of

67
00:02:59,616 --> 00:03:01,591
candidates that are considered at all.

68
00:03:02,121 --> 00:03:03,855
So here it's not about boosting

69
00:03:04,048 --> 00:03:05,718
probabilities, it's simply about

70
00:03:06,296 --> 00:03:07,950
getting rid of some candidates.

71
00:03:08,528 --> 00:03:11,162
For example, if you have a k value of 5,

72
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,005
only the 5 most likely values are

73
00:03:14,005 --> 00:03:16,510
considered. If it's 1, it's definitely the

74
00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:18,437
most likely value that will be used.

75
00:03:19,079 --> 00:03:22,060
So if the top-k parameter were set to 1

76
00:03:22,092 --> 00:03:25,315
here, we would definitely pick blue because

77
00:03:25,315 --> 00:03:29,258
it's the most likely token in this made-up

78
00:03:29,258 --> 00:03:29,915
example here.

79
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:33,907
If I set top-k to 2 instead, for example,

80
00:03:34,356 --> 00:03:36,745
blue and visible would be considered because

81
00:03:36,777 --> 00:03:39,229
these are the 2 highest percentages.

82
00:03:39,823 --> 00:03:43,077
The dot dot dot with 22% is meant to

83
00:03:43,109 --> 00:03:45,898
represent multiple alternatives where each

84
00:03:45,994 --> 00:03:48,045
alternative has less than 22%,

85
00:03:48,702 --> 00:03:49,391
just to be clear.

86
00:03:50,096 --> 00:03:51,281
So that's Top-K.

87
00:03:52,387 --> 00:03:53,428
Top-P

88
00:03:53,989 --> 00:03:56,793
is about limiting the candidates based on

89
00:03:56,793 --> 00:03:58,540
their combined probabilities.

90
00:03:59,357 --> 00:04:02,690
If P is set to 0.5, for example, all

91
00:04:02,898 --> 00:04:05,366
candidates would be considered that combined

92
00:04:05,366 --> 00:04:06,391
have more than 50%.

93
00:04:07,545 --> 00:04:10,237
With 0.9, all candidates that have more than

94
00:04:10,269 --> 00:04:10,653
90%

95
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:11,887
would be considered.

96
00:04:12,673 --> 00:04:16,817
So again, here, if top_p were set to 0.5,

97
00:04:17,476 --> 00:04:20,078
blue and visible would be considered because

98
00:04:20,142 --> 00:04:22,712
combined they have more than 50% and we

99
00:04:22,712 --> 00:04:25,330
don't need any other candidates to go above

100
00:04:25,667 --> 00:04:25,940
50%.

101
00:04:26,952 --> 00:04:29,265
If top_p were set to 90%,

102
00:04:30,261 --> 00:04:33,136
we would need blue, visible, and clear, but

103
00:04:33,136 --> 00:04:35,368
even then we would still be below 90%,

104
00:04:35,947 --> 00:04:37,569
so we would also include some other

105
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:39,832
candidates from those remaining tokens.

106
00:04:40,778 --> 00:04:42,655
And then from all these tokens that are

107
00:04:42,768 --> 00:04:45,222
included in the actual candidates, one

108
00:04:45,351 --> 00:04:47,950
candidate will be chosen. And that will then

109
00:04:48,078 --> 00:04:50,308
be the actual token that makes it into the

110
00:04:50,469 --> 00:04:51,126
actual output.

111
00:04:51,993 --> 00:04:54,479
And by the way, it's not like the highest

112
00:04:54,479 --> 00:04:57,271
probability then always wins. Instead, you

113
00:04:57,287 --> 00:05:00,271
can think of it as a weighted dice roll. So

114
00:05:00,271 --> 00:05:02,549
the higher probability candidate is more

115
00:05:02,662 --> 00:05:05,774
likely to be chosen, but the less likely one

116
00:05:05,951 --> 00:05:07,619
also have a chance of being chosen.

117
00:05:08,277 --> 00:05:10,943
That's how temperature, top-k, and top-p

118
00:05:11,007 --> 00:05:13,833
work, and they can be combined. You can

119
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:16,113
exaggerate and flatten differences with

120
00:05:16,145 --> 00:05:18,505
temperature, then restrict the number of

121
00:05:18,553 --> 00:05:21,026
candidates with top-k, and then in addition

122
00:05:21,203 --> 00:05:23,354
also use top-p, for example.

123
00:05:24,189 --> 00:05:27,625
There also is min-p, and min-p can be used

124
00:05:27,625 --> 00:05:30,275
to discard certain candidates that don't

125
00:05:30,291 --> 00:05:32,651
meet a minimum probability threshold.

126
00:05:33,582 --> 00:05:36,838
So for example, if you set top_k to 5

127
00:05:37,495 --> 00:05:40,446
and you therefore have 5 candidates, you

128
00:05:40,479 --> 00:05:44,376
could in addition set min_p to 0.05 to

129
00:05:44,488 --> 00:05:46,349
remove all candidates that have an

130
00:05:46,413 --> 00:05:49,428
individual probability of less than 5%.

131
00:05:50,919 --> 00:05:53,405
So if one of your 5 candidates would only

132
00:05:53,453 --> 00:05:55,105
have a probability of 4%,

133
00:05:55,715 --> 00:05:59,371
it would be excluded with min_p set to 0.05

134
00:05:59,708 --> 00:06:02,098
even if it would be one of the 5 most likely

135
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:02,419
ones.

136
00:06:03,493 --> 00:06:06,413
That's the idea here. Now, I will say that

137
00:06:06,541 --> 00:06:07,343
in reality,

138
00:06:07,985 --> 00:06:11,145
you likely will not tweak these settings all

139
00:06:11,273 --> 00:06:13,438
the time. The defaults are typically pretty

140
00:06:13,519 --> 00:06:13,727
good,

141
00:06:14,305 --> 00:06:16,775
giving you a nice mixture of creativity,

142
00:06:17,128 --> 00:06:18,427
randomness, and

143
00:06:18,988 --> 00:06:22,357
expected behavior, you could say. But for

144
00:06:22,357 --> 00:06:25,292
specific use cases, you can definitely tweak

145
00:06:25,308 --> 00:06:27,682
these settings. And we will play around with

146
00:06:27,714 --> 00:06:30,040
them to get a better feeling for them in the

147
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:30,746
next lecture.
